{
  "_comment": [
    "THE CLASS OF AN AUDIT EVENT, ANSWERED BY THE DATABASE AND HELD HERE.",
    "",
    "audit_event_class(action, entity_type, audit_domain, old_data, new_data) in",
    "supabase/migrations/0228_the_audit_trail_sorts_events_into_classes_in_the_database.sql decides",
    "which class an Audit Trail event is in: created, operational, configuration, lifecycle or read.",
    "The dashboard draws the marker the server names and holds no copy of the rules.",
    "",
    "supabase/migrations/test_the_audit_trail_sorts_events_into_classes_in_the_database.py asserts",
    "every case below. A case is one audit row as the trail stores it; `class` is the answer.",
    "",
    "`browser` is what the dashboard's own classifier answered before the rules moved to the",
    "server, where that differs. Only the four reads differ, and on purpose: before the Read class",
    "a read was drawn as a configuration change or an operational one."
  ],
